  "summary": "A deaerator removes dissolved oxygen and carbon dioxide from boiler feedwater, which would otherwise corrode the boiler. Incoming water is sprayed into steam and trickles over trays, heating it to saturation; the gases are released and vented, and the hot deaerated water collects in the storage tank.",
